cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it."
title: "Agentic Bioinformatics Research: A Reproducible Environment for LLM-Based Multi-Agent Systems"
authors:
  - family-names: Pesnev
    given-names: Vitaly
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/wevelostdancin/agentic-bioinformatics-research"
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - large language models
  - agent orchestration
  - bioinformatics
  - reproducibility
  - verification
abstract: >-
  A research environment for experiments on orchestration, verification, and
  completeness measurement in LLM-based multi-agent systems applied to
  bioinformatics. The environment fixes dependencies, records provenance and
  structured traces, uses executable evidence gates, and applies statistical
  completeness estimates.
